{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_frjkDplFCMb7kJSmhUpNzy5S","content":"1\t# What the watch showed for event 184233 (Tempo run 45)\n2\t\n3\tIntervals: LTHR 172. Watch (Forerunner 965): auto-detected LTHR 168, zones\n4\tZ1 <118, Z2 118–137, Z3 137–151, Z4 151–162, Z5 >162.\n5\t\n6\t`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/184233` returned the event exactly as we sent\n7\tit (see `event-184233-as-sent.json`); `workout_doc.steps` is populated, so the\n8\tAPI accepted it.\n9\t\n10\t| step | planned (% LTHR) | expected on watch (× 172) | watch displayed |\n11\t|---|---|---|---|\n12\t| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 118–137 |\n13\t| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–162 |\n14\t| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 137–151 |\n15\t| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 118–137 |\n16\t\n17\tEvery corridor shows up as one of the watch's own zone bands, not the range we\n18\tplanned. Changing the watch's LTHR to 172 moves the bands but they are still\n19\tzone edges, never 151–160 or 129–141. Earlier tries: `units: \"bpm\"` with\n20\tabsolute values made the watch show 214–249 bpm; `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` made\n21\tevery target a constant 101."}
